{"id": "EUVD-2026-64529", "enisaUuid": "a0a0fea0-662b-37c7-b6cd-0b3133349b0e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nima: Instantiate file_truncate and path_truncate hooks\n\nInstantiate the file_truncate and path_truncate LSM hooks to reset the\naction cache flags (IMA_DONE_MASK) as soon as truncation is requested,\nso the file, based on policy, is re-collected, re-measured, re-audited,\nand re-appraised on next access.", "datePublished": "2026-08-22T15:31:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:05:59", "baseScore": 8.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5f46705d96eb60587aa7035acfcbec977e08d620", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dd21c96a71e876c8df9ec546b885a2c5f47bbb05", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0baed1fa2184c81e4baf76f445d3faa4b738c8f7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b80bed5c871a80151351342c065579405ce77145"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hgmq-24pq-jx89", "CVE-2026-74592"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.34, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "019bab09-d232-3c7a-af07-fbbd8261d851", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.104"}, {"id": "02264a86-8c71-3f2b-bd10-666b749defcb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3323eec921efd815178a23107ab63588c605c0b2 <0baed1fa2184c81e4baf76f445d3faa4b738c8f7"}, {"id": "30d3d150-e30a-345c-9621-e940be6a90cf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.30"}, {"id": "3ce247f4-7ccb-3dd9-8232-3c35a641f1dc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3323eec921efd815178a23107ab63588c605c0b2 <dd21c96a71e876c8df9ec546b885a2c5f47bbb05"}, {"id": "3d733c23-5ccf-3ce4-83da-42c22c6acbea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3323eec921efd815178a23107ab63588c605c0b2 <b80bed5c871a80151351342c065579405